{
  "id": "ai.owner.v1",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": {
    "en": "The owner's AI (W-AI). Provider layer: the owner's own OpenAI-compatible endpoint + key (OpenRouter free models are the documented default, each owner pastes THEIR key; the platform holds none) -> Cloudflare Workers AI through the Worker's [ai] binding within a per-venue daily share of the account's 10,000 free neurons (ai.spent, cap AI_VENUE_NEURONS, default 300) -> 'AI is off' with the reason. Nothing is sent while ai.enabled is off; the test button sends only 'OK?'. Q&A: a question becomes ONE query from a closed list of 16 kinds (lexicon in sq/en/uk/ru, else the model picks and query::validate refuses anything else); the number is read from /fold/analytics or /fold/kitchen -- the same answers /api/owner/analytics[?/kitchen] serve -- and every number carries its source route, the JSON pointers it sums and the days whose records it covers. Sentences are templates; a model rewording is shown only if it keeps every number and adds none. Explain cards for the analytics and kitchen screens. No person is ever a query (no scoring); facts to /api/owner/assist stay redacted. The key is never in any response body (keySet only; provider errors scrubbed).",
    "uk": "ШІ власника: власний ключ (OpenRouter безкоштовно) -> Workers AI у межах денної частки закладу -> вимкнено; числа лише з фолдів аналітики, кожне з джерелом і записами; ключ ніколи не повертається."
  },
